A||||5||84Bill||Side windows / door glass||||14||
Z||000000||84Bill||06-25-2001||02:26 PM||||You all will be happy to know I actually went outside this weekend and last, well sort of if you consider a garage outside. <BR>My side window glass came in this weekend 160 bucks for both. I have new outer wipes and windows now all I need is the inner wipes. I never noticed how scratched up the windows were until I looked through the new ones. The passenger window regulator was running very slow and I found out the grease had turned into a stiff gummy substance that I had a hard time removing even with engine degreaser! Even the door latch was a mess so I removed it to give it a good cleaning. I spent the rest of the day sanding the fender and hood. Go check it out. <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Indy.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||poupas||06-25-2001||02:44 PM||||I just had to post in your thread.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bzzzted||06-25-2001||03:17 PM||||any good instructions on replaceing side glass?, my driver door was stripped but have all the parts to put it back together just need some good instructions before i dive in and the Hayes manual doesn't cover this very well except adjustment once the glass is in||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-25-2001||05:26 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bzzzted:<BR><B>any good instructions on replaceing side glass?, my driver door was stripped but have all the parts to put it back together just need some good instructions before i dive in and the Hayes manual doesn't cover this very well except adjustment once the glass is in</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have not put mine back together yet. The best way I can see is to put the track and window channel parts back in first then put the glass in then put the bump stops in last. One thing make sure you put the nose channel piece back in the faward hole in the glass before you put the window in the door.<P>As far as adjusting the window <BR>1 roll the window all the way up to where it fits snugg at the to and all the wat around the seal. <BR>2 Adjust the front and rear bump stops down so they just touch then tighten them.<BR>3 Roll the  window down then back up to see if is stopping at the right spot if it is not then lower the window a bit and readjust the offending stop.<P>4 Once you have that set tighten the window guide bolts with the window up and door closed. then tighten the felt coverd guides on the top inside part of the door.<P>If all the hardware is tight on the window and the window is firmly held in it's track the process is very easy, I have made adjustments to other windows but not to ones I have completely removed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>FYI<BR>I don't know how many of us suffer the imfamous window creak when the window is 1/2 way down. I found that the rivits had loosend up and allowed the window to move just slightly in it's mount causing it to rub the bottom of the lip and make the creaking noise.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/op/mount.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||007DOUG||06-26-2001||08:23 AM||||Always glad to see someone saving an indy.<P>Noticed it came from NJ. I probably looked at that Indy once before years ago. Two of my indys have come from NJ.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>2 86 Red GTs (twins) <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT Blue w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT Pearl White 3.4 T-top<BR>88 Faded red Formula 5 speed<BR>2 Black 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||14
